A||||7||Gokart||What is this?||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||08-10-2000||10:08 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ag10$001_2.jpg">  Is there scheduled maitenence that needs to be done to it? Does the cover come off to check fluid? I've had my GT 18 months now and haven't touched it yet!<P>Marc 87GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||08-11-2000||12:06 AM||||Sensor for the Vehicle Speed Sensor.  Can't tell if you have an auto or 5 speed, but both of them have a dipstick to check fluid level.  Unless it goes out you don't have to touch it.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||08-11-2000||01:59 AM||||When I checked mine, it was sort of low, so you might want to just pull it off and check (the dipstick is actually on the bottom of that thing, if the last message wasn't too clear). It's only held on by an 11mm or 10mm (can't remember) Hope that helps.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||08-11-2000||05:20 AM||||What are the steps to removing it? I'm sure the first is to unplug the sensor wire but where is the 11mm/10mm bolt/nut? Does this sensor come straight out or does it unscrew out. What kind of fluid do you fill it with if it's low? Thanks!<P>Marc 87GT<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 08-11-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000004||Standard||08-11-2000||05:51 AM||||So far as I know, the only tranny's that you had to pull the speed sensor to check the fluid level in was the 4 speeds.  All the others had a dipstick mounted elsewhere. <P>What kind of tranny do you have,  Gokart?<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||08-11-2000||06:27 AM||||5-spd Standard(87GT)! Thanks for replying again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Should I leave it be? Where do I check the fluid for the speed sensor then if not here?<P>Marc 87GT <p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 08-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Taijiguy||08-11-2000||08:03 AM||||Gokart-<BR>You don't need to check anything with the speed sensor exceept ocassionally maybe what it's reporting to the speedometer! (meaning check your speed once in a while buy looking at the speedo......never mind...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<BR>The only service you need to do with the trans at all is to check the fluid when you do a tune-up. There's a screw-in dipstick located more or less behind that speed sensor. The dipstick has a broad flat tab sticking up that you can grab to unscrew it.<BR>If you get really ambitious some day, you might change the oil out in the trans, but get a book for that so you know where the drain plug is located.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||08-11-2000||12:47 PM||||if your <B>really</B> curious to see whats underneath it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  frst unplug the connector, then you will need a 10mm socket to remove the screw... be carefull not to lose the retaining clip that holds it in place.<P>thirdly... <B>BE VERY CAREFULL</B> pullling it out.  there is a little red gear wheel on the bottom (this makes contact with another gear to record the speed). if you bump it and it falls off... you have to go a fishing!<P>examine it, look at it, and carefully reverse the above steps to reinstall it.<P>btw, this is an excellent place to fill the fluid in the tranny.  it is easier to get to, and provides a larger opening for a funnel.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
